citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Zhang</surname><given-names>ZG</given-names></name><name><surname>Yu</surname><given-names>WG</given-names></name><name><surname>Qiu</surname><given-names>WS</given-names></name><name><surname>Zhao</surname><given-names>HM</given-names></name></person-group><year>2006</year><article-title>Immunogenicity of C-terminus of Plasmodium falciparum merozoite surface protein 1 expressed as a non-glycosylated polypeptide in yeast.</article-title><source>Acta Biochim Biophys Sin (Shanghai)</source><volume>38</volume><fpage>403</fpage><lpage>409</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16761098</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0001063-Giersing1"><label>16</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Giersing</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Miura</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Shimp</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Wang</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Zhou</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2005</year><article-title>posttranslational modification of recombinant Plasmodium falciparum apical membrane antigen 1: impact on functional immune responses to a malaria vaccine candidate.</article-title><source>Infect Immun</source><volume>73</volume><fpage>3963</fpage><lpage>3970</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15972483</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0001063-Mahanty1"><label>17</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Mahanty</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Saul</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Miller</surname><given-names>LH</given-names></name></person-group><year>2003</year><article-title>Progress in the development of recombinant and synthetic blood-stage malaria vaccines.</article-title><source>